{"availability":"available","full":"celox-sim/celox","name":"celox","description":"Celox HDL Simulator","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":10,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-28T11:52:19Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:57:42Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://celox-sim.github.io/celox/","topics":[],"demo":"https://celox-sim.github.io/celox/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:42.318Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:42.318Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:42.318Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:41.081Z","stars":10,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","stars":10,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:24.644Z","stars":10,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:21.660Z","stars":10,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-11T00:23:10.696Z","stars":10,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:42.318Z","stars":10,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A compiler-based RTL simulator for Veryl and a synthesizable subset of SystemVerilog.","Celox compiles an elaborated Veryl design into executable simulation kernels and exposes the design through a type-safe TypeScript API. The same kernels can be built from synthesizable SystemVerilog through the Rust API (see SystemVerilog support). It is both a practical way to test RTL with Vitest and an open testbed for exploring how RTL simulators should be structured.","Celox explores a simple question: what does a modern RTL simulator architecture look like when compilation, scheduling, state representation, code generation, and testbench integration are designed together?"],"features":["Veryl-specific analysis ends at a source-independent design representation.","Combinational dependencies and clock domains are scheduled before execution.","A backend-independent IR and state layout are shared by multiple code","Native and WebAssembly execution use the same runtime contract.","The testbench sees the same typed design API re